   "source": {
    "label": "thm:main",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Let Assumptions \\ref{ass:set_bound}, \\ref{ass:bounded} and \\ref{ass:noise} hold. Then, with probability at least $1 - \\delta$, the regret of ROFUL (Algorithm \\ref{alg:main_alg}) satisfies R_T \\leq 2 \\frac{\\|\\theta \\| + S_a}{b} \\beta_T \\sqrt{2 d T \\log\\left(1 + \\frac{T}{\\lambda d} \\right)}, and $a^\\top x_t \\leq b$ for all $t \\in [T]$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Pseudo-regret bounded w.p. 1-delta. Theorem 4 restates it as 2(||theta||/b + 1/nu) beta_T sqrt(...), identical since 1/nu = S_a/b. Also guarantees constraint satisfaction every round. Order O(d sqrt(T) log T / b)."
  },
